		<item>
			<title>Rai News 24 commercial featuring Big Daddy cover of Madonna Like a Virgin</title>
			<link>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/797-rai-news-24-commercial-featuring-big-daddy-cover-of-madonna-like-a-virgin.html</link>
			<guid>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/797-rai-news-24-commercial-featuring-big-daddy-cover-of-madonna-like-a-virgin.html</guid>
			<description><![CDATA[<div class="K2FeedIntroText"><p>A brand new commercial for Italian national all news channel <a href="http://www.rainews24.rai.it/" target="_blank" title="rai news 24 madonna like a virgin"><strong>Rai News 24</strong></a> features <strong>Big Daddy</strong> cover of <strong>Madonna's Like a Virgin</strong>.</p>
<p> </p>
<p>The track was included in <strong>Big Daddy</strong>'s Cutting Their Own Groove album. His version of Like a Virgin includes a sample of Frankie Avalon's Venus. You can heard him singing lines like "Madonna, material girl come to me..."</p>
<p> </p>
<p>Do you like this version? Post your comments below...</p>
<p> </p>
<p>{youtube}Hsdgm3A9VKo{/youtube}</p></div>]]></description>
			<category>TV</category>
			<pubDate>Wed, 10 Oct 2012 17:42:20 +0000</pubDate>
		</item>
		<item>
			<title>Bimbo Jones and Eddie Amador did Official Remixes for Madonna Superstar</title>
			<link>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/796-bimbo-jones-and-eddie-amador-did-official-remixes-for-madonna-superstar.html</link>
			<guid>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/796-bimbo-jones-and-eddie-amador-did-official-remixes-for-madonna-superstar.html</guid>
			<description><![CDATA[<div class="K2FeedIntroText"><p>As rumoured, Live Nation and Interscope Records are taking <strong>Superstar</strong> in consideration as <strong>Madonna</strong>'s next single.</p>
<p> </p>
<p>Last months we reported that, besides Turn Up The Radio, <strong>Madonna</strong> wanted to release Gang Bang. Now we hear that, also due to the Bravo campaign in the USA, <strong>Superstar</strong> is being taken in consideration.</p>
<p> </p>
<p>But most of all, we heard that there are already <strong>Official Remixes</strong> that have been done for <strong>Superstar</strong>.</p>
<p>DrownedMadonna.com learnt that <strong>Bimbo Jones</strong> and <strong>Eddie Amador</strong> did official remixes for Madonna's Superstar.</p></div>]]></description>
			<category>Music</category>
			<pubDate>Mon, 08 Oct 2012 09:12:46 +0000</pubDate>
		</item>
		<item>
			<title>Madonna celebrates her 30 year career performing Everybody in San Jose</title>
			<link>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/795-madonna-celebrates-her-30-year-career-performing-everybody-in-san-jose.html</link>
			<guid>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/795-madonna-celebrates-her-30-year-career-performing-everybody-in-san-jose.html</guid>
			<description><![CDATA[<div class="K2FeedIntroText"><p>{youtube}ZITL6kGYnEg{/youtube}</p>
<p> </p>
<p>Last night <strong>Madonn</strong>a performed her first sing <strong>Everybody</strong>, which was released exactly 30 years ago on October 6 1983, during her <strong>MDNA</strong> show in <strong>San Jose</strong>.</p></div>]]></description>
			<category>Music</category>
			<pubDate>Sun, 07 Oct 2012 11:04:49 +0000</pubDate>
		</item>
		<item>
			<title>Madonna... 25 years ago in Turin, Italy</title>
			<link>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/794-madonna-25-years-ago-in-turin-italy.html</link>
			<guid>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/794-madonna-25-years-ago-in-turin-italy.html</guid>
			<description><![CDATA[<div class="K2FeedIntroText"><p>It was 25 years last night. It was not only a concert, but most of all a huge event in Italy, which broke every record on Italian TV. The whole country was in front of the TV to watch the show live from Turin. Madonna's Italian speeches are still iconic.</p>
<p> </p>
<p>{youtube}ScKEtna52-I{/youtube}</p></div>]]></description>
			<category>Tours</category>
			<pubDate>Wed, 05 Sep 2012 00:00:33 +0000</pubDate>
		</item>
		<item>
			<title>Vote for Monte Pittman remix of Bon Ivery Calgary</title>
			<link>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/793-vote-for-monte-pittman-remix-of-bon-ivery-calgary.html</link>
			<guid>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/793-vote-for-monte-pittman-remix-of-bon-ivery-calgary.html</guid>
			<description><![CDATA[<div class="K2FeedIntroText"><p><strong>Monte Pittman</strong>, <strong>Madonna</strong>’s guitar player and  guitar teacher, has submitted his remix of <strong>Bon Iver’s song “Calgary”</strong> to the <a href="http://www.indabamusic.com/opportunities/bon-iver-bon-iver-stems-project-calgary/submissions/130163"> indabamusic.com</a> contest. <span lang="EN-US">MDNA Tour band mate Brian Frasier-Moore is  on drums and Monte plays guitar. </span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-US"><br /></span></p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-US">We would deeply appreciate it if you could  vote for Monte. <a href="http://www.indabamusic.com/opportunities/bon-iver-bon-iver-stems-project-calgary/submissions/130163">Click here</a> to vote him.</span></p>
<p> </p>
<p>
<object id="playlist-widget" width="690" height="190">
<param name="movie" value="http://embed.indabamusic.com/playlist.swf?height=190&amp;uuid=c719ad2a-f2b7-11e1-a4e5-1231390e6561&amp;width=690" />
<param name="allowScriptAccess" value="always" />
<param name="wmode" value="transparent" /> <embed type="application/x-shockwave-flash" width="690" height="190" src="http://embed.indabamusic.com/playlist.swf?height=190&amp;uuid=c719ad2a-f2b7-11e1-a4e5-1231390e6561&amp;width=690" allowscriptaccess="always" flashvars="height=190&amp;uuid=c719ad2a-f2b7-11e1-a4e5-1231390e6561&amp;width=690" quality="high" wmode="transparent"></embed>
</object>
</p></div>]]></description>
			<category>Music</category>
			<pubDate>Sun, 02 Sep 2012 10:36:28 +0000</pubDate>
		</item>
		<item>
			<title>Madonna MDNA Show Manifesto about violence and guns on her tour</title>
			<link>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/792-madonna-mdna-show-manifesto-about-violence-and-guns-on-her-tour.html</link>
			<guid>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/792-madonna-mdna-show-manifesto-about-violence-and-guns-on-her-tour.html</guid>
			<description><![CDATA[<div class="K2FeedIntroText"><p><strong>Madonna</strong> released a statement today - called the <strong>MDNA Show Manifesto</strong> - defending her use of prop guns in her <strong>MDNA tour</strong> and  explaining some of its other imagery. She sent it out to a few people who are  reviewing the show and we can post it thanks to <a href="http://www.metro.us/philadelphia/local/article/1150671--mdna-show-manifesto-madonna-releases-a-statement-defending-the-use-of-guns-on-her-world-tour" target="_blank" title="madonna mdna show manifesto">Metro Philadelphia</a>, where you can read more.</p>
<p> </p>
<p><em>My show<br style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Trebuchet MS'; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 16px; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: #ffffff;" />Is a journey.<br style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Trebuchet MS'; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 16px; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: #ffffff;" />The journey of a soul from darkness to light<br style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Trebuchet MS'; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 16px; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: #ffffff;" />It is part   cinematic musical  theatre.<br style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Trebuchet MS'; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 16px; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: #ffffff;" />Part spectacle and sometimes  intimate  Performance art.<br style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Trebuchet MS'; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 16px; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: #ffffff;" /><br style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Trebuchet MS'; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 16px; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: #ffffff;" />But above all  its a journey</em> <em><br style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Trebuchet MS'; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 16px; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: #ffffff;" />From darkness to light<br style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Trebuchet MS'; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 16px; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: #ffffff;" />From anger to love<br style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Trebuchet MS'; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 16px; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: #ffffff;" />from chaos to order.<br style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Trebuchet MS'; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 16px; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: #ffffff;" /><br style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Trebuchet MS'; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 16px; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: #ffffff;" />It's true there is a lot of violence in the beginning of the show and sometimes the use of fake guns - but they are used as metaphors.<br style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Trebuchet MS'; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 16px; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: #ffffff;" />I do not condone violence or the use of guns.<br style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Trebuchet MS'; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 16px; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: #ffffff;" />Rather they are symbols of wanting to appear strong and wanting to find a way to stop feelings  that I find hurtful or damaging.   In my case its wanting to stop the lies and hypocrisy of the church,  the intolerance of many narrow minded cultures and societies I have experienced throughout my life<br style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Trebuchet MS'; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 16px; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: #ffffff;" />and in some cases  the pain I have felt from having my heart broken.<br style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Trebuchet MS'; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 16px; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: #ffffff;" /><br style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Trebuchet MS'; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 16px; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: #ffffff;" /> Ultimately as we  follow through the journey of my story,  the audience can  see quite clearly  what I see - That the enemy is within and the only way to survive Disappointment Disapproval Judgment Heartbreak Jealousy Envy And Hatred Is with Love -  not with revenge -  not with guns and not with violence.<br style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Trebuchet MS'; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 16px; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: #ffffff;" /><br style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Trebuchet MS'; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 16px; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: #ffffff;" />In spite of all the chaos and darkness and intolerance we seem to be encountering more and more in the world, We cannot allow our anger or bitterness to swallow us up.<br style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Trebuchet MS'; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 16px; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: #ffffff;" />We  come to understand that<br style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Trebuchet MS'; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 16px; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: #ffffff;" />There is an innate and pure love inside us all and we have to find a way to tap into it.<br style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Trebuchet MS'; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 16px; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: #ffffff;" /><br style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Trebuchet MS'; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 16px; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: #ffffff;" />And we can't do it by being victims or placing the blame or pointing the finger at  others.<br style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Trebuchet MS'; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 16px; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: #ffffff;" />But by recognizing that the enemy is within And when we come to terms with it And accept it And struggle to change ourselves, Then we can change the world without hurting anyone and  we can inspire others to do the same.<br style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Trebuchet MS'; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 16px; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: #ffffff;" /><br style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Trebuchet MS'; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 16px; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: #ffffff;" />When you watch a film there are usually good guys and bad guys to help illustrate this point, Sometimes I play both.</em> <em><br style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Trebuchet MS'; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 16px; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: #ffffff;" />I enjoy acting out this journey.<br style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Trebuchet MS'; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 16px; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: #ffffff;" />For none of us are perfect and we all have our own journey of growth to go on.<br style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Trebuchet MS'; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 16px; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: #ffffff;" /><br style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Trebuchet MS'; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 16px; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: #ffffff;" />I know people can relate to it.</em> <em><br style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Trebuchet MS'; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 16px; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: #ffffff;" />It's very important to me as an artist  that my show not be taken out of context.<br style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Trebuchet MS'; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 16px; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: #ffffff;" /><br style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Trebuchet MS'; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 16px; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: #ffffff;" />It must be watched with an open heart from beginning to end. I am sure if it is viewed this way,  the viewer will walk away feeling inspired,  Invigorated and will want to make the world a better place.<br style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Trebuchet MS'; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 16px; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: #ffffff;" /><br style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Trebuchet MS'; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 16px; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: #ffffff;" />And this of course was always my intention.<br style="color: #000000; font-family: 'Trebuchet MS'; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 16px; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: #ffffff;" /> </em></p>
<p><strong><em>-Madonna</em></strong></p></div>]]></description>
			<category>Tours</category>
			<pubDate>Tue, 28 Aug 2012 07:55:38 +0000</pubDate>
		</item>
		<item>
			<title>Madonna speech: 'We are entering some scaring time in the world and people become intollerant!'</title>
			<link>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/791-madonna-speech-we-are-entering-some-scaring-time-in-the-world-and-people-become-intollerant.html</link>
			<guid>http://drownedmadonna.com/index/item/791-madonna-speech-we-are-entering-some-scaring-time-in-the-world-and-people-become-intollerant.html</guid>
			<description><![CDATA[<div class="K2FeedIntroText"><p>{youtube}k9oY5G-Imww{/youtube}"</p>
<p> </p>
<p>We are entering some very scaring time in the world. Cconomic markets  are collapsing. People are nothing to eat in Greece. People all over the  world are suffering and people are afraid. And, what happens when  people are afraid? They become intollerant! they start pointing the  fingers at other people. They say:<em> 'you are the reason, you are the  problem, you are to blame!'</em> they say: <em>'get out!'</em> And this  of course, you know, it's not the answer to the problem. The enemy is  not out there. There is no such thing as an external enemy. The enemy is  within. I know that I have made a certain Marine Le Pene very angry  with me... and, it's not my intention to make enemies. It's my intention  to PROMOTE TOLLERANCE. This is my intention. [..] You know? If we don't  learn from history, we would just repeat it. So, the next time you want  to point the finger at somebody, and blame them for your problems in  your life, take that finger and point it back at you! And fix it! If you  see a problem, don't complain, fix it!"</p></div>]]></description>
			<category>Tours</category>
			<pubDate>Thu, 26 Jul 2012 23:58:32 +0000</pubDate>
		</item>
